    <DataNode elementId="AT3G45070-MONOMER" textLabel="sulfotransferase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9M1V2" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="415" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">A flavonoid 7-sulfotransferase from &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt;, AtST3a, was cloned and characterized. The recombinant protein exhibited strict specificity for position 7 of flavonoids. However, unlike the flavonoid 7-sulfotransferase from &lt;i&gt; Flaveria bidentis &lt;/i&gt; |CITS: [7991681]|, AtST3a was found to accept a number of flavonols and flavone aglycones, as well as their monosulfate esters as substrates |CITS: [17095238]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT3G45070-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT3G45070.2" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q9M1V2" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="AT3G45070.2" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-16205" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT3G45070.2" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT3G45070" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_7991681" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_17095238" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT4G26220-MONOMER" textLabel="Probable caffeoyl-CoA O-methyltransferase At4g26220" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9C5D7" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="450" centerY="415" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The |FRAME: AT4G26220 CCoAOMT7| (AT4G26220) gene of |FRAME: ORG-5993 &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; col| belongs to a group of Mg&lt;sup&gt;2+&lt;/sup&gt;-dependent low molecular weight (2327 kDa) methyltransferases with a preference for caffeoyl coenzyme A esters known as CCoAOMTs. The gene was cloned and functionally expressed in |FRAME: TAX-562 &lt;i&gt;Escherichia coli&lt;/i&gt;|, and the recombinant protein was purified to homogeneity |CITS: [23416302]|. The purified protein was able to methylate |FRAME: CAFFEOYL-COA &lt;i&gt;trans&lt;/i&gt;-caffeoyl-CoA| as expected, but was much more active with |FRAME: 5734-TETRAHYDROXYFLAVONE luteolin| (3-fold) and |FRAME: CPD-520 quercetin| (2-fold). The enzyme was also active with the flavanone |FRAME: CPD-6994 (2S)-eriodictyol| (at half the activity with |FRAME: CAFFEOYL-COA &lt;i&gt;trans&lt;/i&gt;-caffeoyl-CoA|). Rather unusally, the enzyme could methylate this substrate at either the 3&apos; or 4&apos; positions,forming |FRAME: CPD-7071 homoeriodictyol| and |FRAME: CPD-7072 (2S)-hesperetin|, respectively |CITS: [23416302]|. The was used as part of an engineered pathway for the production of |FRAME: SCOPOLETIN scopoletin| |CITS: [23644174]|. The recombinant E. coli strain was able to produce 6.6 mg/L |FRAME: SCOPOLETIN scopoletin| in 60 h when 1 mM |FRAME: CPD-676 &lt;i&gt;trans&lt;/i&gt;-caffeate| was fed, indicating that the enzyme is functional &lt;i&gt;in vivo&lt;/i&gt; and can utilize the |FRAME: TAX-562 &lt;i&gt;Escherichia coli&lt;/i&gt;| endogenous |FRAME: S-ADENOSYLMETHIONINE &lt;i&gt;S&lt;/i&gt;-adenosyl-L-methionine| as the methyl donor.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT4G26220-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT4G26220.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pride" value="Q9C5D7" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Smr" value="Q9C5D7" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Panther" value="PTHR10509" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Prosite" value="PS51682" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pfam" value="PF01596" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Interpro" value="IPR029063" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q9C5D7" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="Trans-caffeoyl-CoA 3-O-methyltransferase" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="CCoAMT" />
      <Property key="Synonym_3" value="CCoAOMT" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-22245, RXN-22246, RXN-22247, RXN-22248, RXN-32911, RXN-32910, RXN-32909, RXN-32908, RXN-32907, RXN-32906, RXN-30485" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="11" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT4G26220.1" />
